From 36b60ad909804668ca4cd9071724080bfa2a9771 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:45:17 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18f: attach extension tab helpers to registry
 tabs

Give browser-less kTabContents tabs Chromium's extension tab helpers as TabHelpers attaches them: the extension view type, extensions::TabHelper (ScriptExecutor, ExtensionActionRunner, ActiveTabPermissionGranter), a SessionTabHelper without a SessionService delegate (extension tab IDs, no window session state) and WebNavigationTabObserver. ExtensionTabUtil::GetTabById resolves open registry tabs to contents only (no WindowController, TAB_INDEX_NONE), as it already does for prerendered tabs, so scripting.executeScript, tabs.sendMessage and webNavigation reach them. Registry tabs stay outside tabs.query/windows.*. ABI 1.31 / bridge 0.33.0 (extension_tab_helpers); build p78, native content script, runtime messaging with sender.tab, webNavigation, tabs.sendMessage, executeScript by tab ID and OTR non-injection pass with a local --load-extension fixture.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
